                <pb facs="0571" n="485" sameAs="frus:frus1873p1v1/pg485"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center">[From the Hawaiian Gazette of Wednesday, December 11,
                    1872.]</p>
                <p>The health of His Majesty has been failing for some time, and during the last
                    night he experienced a very severe attack, from which, however, he rallied
                    sufficiently to encourage the hopes of his attendants. But at 10 o’clock an
                    unfavorable change took place, and at 20 minutes after 10 o’clock he breathed
                    his last without suffering.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <list>
                            <item>F. W. HUCHISON.</item>
                            <item>STEPHEN H. PHILLIPS.</item>
                            <item>ROBERT STIRLING.</item>
                        </list>
                    </signed>
                    <lb/>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left"><placeName type="venue"><hi
                                rendition="#small-caps">Iolani Palace</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1872-12-11"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 11, 1872</date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>(The order summoning the legislative assembly is printed as an inclosure to
                        Mr. Peirce’s No. 177, of January 10, 1873.)</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
